WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
You've seen what we can do with one call.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.440
Here's what happens when you connect all of them.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.000
Primal reads across your winning calls,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.600
pulls out the non-negotiables, and uses that same standard

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.840
to rate future calls, role play, and coaching.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.880
One bar everywhere.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.240
When you connect Fathom, Fireflies,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.720
or another recorder to Primal, we pull in your call library.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.240
Then we sort the conversations by outcome

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.800
and segment them by market, deal size, and sales stage,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.440
so you're comparing the right calls against each other.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.800
From there, Primal looks across the calls you've won

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.760
and finds the patterns.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.240
The questions your best reps ask.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.600
The objections they handle differently.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.240
The moments where deals turn.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.000
Not theory, your data.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.920
Then it turns those patterns into something

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.240
your team can actually use.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.760
First, the non-negotiables.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.680
The things that have to be present on every call

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.040
pulled straight out of the calls you already won.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.760
From that point on, every future call

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.680
can be rated against them.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.200
The same standard shows up in role play,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.160
so reps can rehearse against the same bar.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.760
And it shows up in coaching, so feedback

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.960
stays tied to what your winning calls already proved.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.640
It also gives your team a training course built

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.320
from your own conversations and a script grounded

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.000
in the language and moves that fit your sales process.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.760
The free review showed you one call.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.360
This shows you what it looks like when your team's calls

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.280
start building a shared standard.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.520
Start your free 14-day trial or book a walkthrough.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.560
The links are right below this video.
